wb-vout-watchdog (1.2.0) stable; urgency=medium

  * Publish nothing while the MQTT broker is away: the replayed backlog of Vin
    samples and heartbeats made mosquitto answer "Quota exceeded" on reconnect;
    the current state is republished on every connect as before
  * Exit with 2 when the broker rejects the MQTT login instead of retrying it
  * Add -c/--config; the confed schema no longer accepts zero periods
  * Report when the retained topics cannot be removed at stop because the
    broker is not connected
  * Depend on python3-paho-mqtt >= 2.1: the unix-socket transport the service
    connects to mosquitto through exists since paho 2.1

 -- Ekaterina Volkova <ekaterina.volkova@wirenboard.com>  Thu, 17 Sep 2026 16:00:36 +0000

wb-vout-watchdog (1.1.0) stable; urgency=medium

  * Drop the python3-libgpiod dependency: the Vout line is driven through the
    kernel's GPIO character device (v2 uAPI) straight from the standard library,
    so the package installs offline on images that do not carry it.
  * Start wb-mqtt-gpio back with --no-block after a lost race for the line, so
    the recovery no longer waits out a systemd ordering deadlock.

 -- Petr Krasnoshchekov <petr.krasnoshchekov@wirenboard.com>  Thu, 13 Aug 2026 12:40:39 +0000

wb-vout-watchdog (1.0.0) stable; urgency=medium

